<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lichtensteig</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lichtensteig is a small town in the canton of St Gallen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thur">Thur</a> in the Toggenburg valley. Founded by the counts of Toggenburg in the 13th century below their castle, it was the chief town of the valley, and after the Abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Saint Gall</a> bought the county in 1468 it became the seat of the abbey's governors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lichtensteig.jpg" alt="Lichtensteig" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: böhringer friedrich · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lichtensteig_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
